# Copy to .env beside compose.yml. Everything here is optional.
# The node's name, AI, the identity provider, notifications, retention, upload size and branding
# are set in Settings → This node, not here.

# ---- Reaching the node ------------------------------------------------------
# The address other devices use, which invite links carry; install.sh sets it to this machine's.
# Browsers may call from PUBLIC_ORIGIN and EXTRA_ORIGINS.
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN=http://192.168.1.10:8787
# The host address the port is published on (default every address); 127.0.0.1 keeps it to this machine.
# HOST_BIND=127.0.0.1
# The published port; PUBLIC_ORIGIN has to name it too.
# HOST_PORT=9000
# Further origins browsers may call from. Minted links stay on PUBLIC_ORIGIN.
# EXTRA_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8787

# ---- Sample workspaces ------------------------------------------------------
# Where Create a workspace finds its samples: a mirror, for a network without internet access.
# SAMPLES_URL=https://github.com/stuga-dev/samples/releases

# ---- Search -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Embedding width, fixed when the database is created; the node refuses to start on a mismatch.
# AI_EMBED_DIMS=1024

# ---- Backups ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Where backups go (default ./backups): the node's own, and ./stuga backup's. How many are kept.
# BACKUP_DIR=/mnt/backups/stuga
# BACKUP_KEEP=7
